    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0806" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2123</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Van Dyke</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-15T17:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 15, 1915, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.40 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>376. Public opinion in the Netherlands thinks Germany is fooling with the United
                    States. German officials here have declared in conversation “feeling in Berlin
                    does not care a dash what the United States say. They can do nothing.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Van Dyke</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
